reconcile_capability dry run: agent-platform on hub gopher, as jane
Order: heron, kestrel

heron: enabled
  Files (1 update, 27 unchanged):
    CHANGE  REPOSITORY                   PATH
    update  giantswarm/oakridge-configs  installations/heron/apps/agent-platform/configmap-values.yaml.patch
  Warning: this reconcile changes what heron's muster serves beyond the shared defaults:
    public-registration redirect URIs added: https://gateway.oakridge.example/oauth/callback (moved from kestrel)
  Includes: giantswarm/oakridge-management-clusters:management-clusters/heron/extras/kustomization.yaml resources ./agent-platform/ (unchanged)
  Includes: giantswarm/oakridge-management-clusters:management-clusters/heron/extras/kustomization.yaml resources ./mcp-kubernetes/ (unchanged)
  Includes: giantswarm/oakridge-management-clusters:management-clusters/heron/extras/kustomization.yaml resources ./mcp-prometheus/ (unchanged)
  Includes: giantswarm/oakridge-management-clusters:management-clusters/heron/extras/kustomization.yaml resources ./mcp-capi/ (unchanged)
  Dex clients:
    00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003: client muster; secretRef dex-client-muster
    : client mcpKubernetes; secretRef dex-client-mcp-kubernetes
    : client mcpPrometheus; secretRef dex-client-mcp-prometheus
    : client mcpCapi; secretRef dex-client-mcp-capi
    kagent: kagent-ui; secretRef dex-client-kagent; redirect URIs https://kagent.heron.oakridge.example/oauth2/callback
  Customer actions:
    heron: Create Secret kagent-anthropic-key in namespace kagent with key ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, or add a ModelConfig in the portal; until then default-model-config (ModelConfig.kagent.dev) stays Accepted=False. (the model key is the installation's own: the definition references the Secret and renders no value for it, and no value is supplied at commit; until the Secret exists the verify reads the runtime feature as waiting for the customer)
  Probes:
    live-oauth2-proxy-extra-audience: identity oauth2-proxy --oidc-extra-audience argument
    live-muster-trusted-audiences: identity muster ConfigMap trustedAudiences
    live-muster-connector-and-client-id: identity muster ConfigMap dex connectorId, where the definition renders one
    live-kagent-api-protected: identity /api/agents answered 403 by oauth2-proxy
    live-kagent-login-redirect: identity /oauth2/start 302 to Dex with client_id=kagent
    live-dex-auth-per-client: identity Dex knows every rendered client and its redirect URI: the connector its /auth answer names answers 302 or its login form
    live-dex-client-secrets-loaded: identity Dex started after every referenced client Secret last changed its data, for every client of the dex patch with a secret reference
    live-oauth2-proxy-audience: identity no audience mismatch in oauth2-proxy's log
    live-oauth2-proxy-secret-and-flux-sa: secrets Secret kagent-oauth2-proxy-credentials and ServiceAccount kagent-flux
    live-model-configs: runtime ModelConfigs in the kagent namespace
    live-kagent-provider-values: runtime kagent HelmRelease .spec.values.providers
    live-konfiguration-source: runtime Konfiguration agent-platform-konfiguration on its GitRepository's revision: behind within its reconciliation interval reads rolling, longer drifted
    live-helmreleases-ready: runtime HelmReleases agent-platform, kagent, connectivity, muster, mcps Ready
    live-platform-workloads: runtime the Deployments that read muster's credentials Available: muster, its Valkey, and klaus-gateway, agent-manager, cluster-manager and model-manager where each runs
    live-kagent-workloads: runtime kagent pods Running and the CNPG cluster healthy
    live-pod-certificate-request: runtime certificates.k8s.io/v1beta1 podcertificaterequests served by the apiserver (Agent Substrate's feature gates, the 4 line)
    live-drift: runtime live values equal the rendered manifests
    live-own-mcp-servers: tool-access MCPServer objects of the installation itself
    live-registered-mcp-servers: tool-access MCPServer objects registered under extras/agent-platform/mcpservers, present and none Failed
    live-muster-protected-resource: tool-access muster's OAuth protected-resource metadata

kestrel: enabled
  A commit would be refused: kestrel's muster serves a registry of its own: its agent-platform values list in-cluster servers of its own (http://mcp-kubernetes.mcp-kubernetes.svc:8080/mcp, http://mcp-prometheus.mcp-prometheus.svc:8080/mcp, http://mcp-capi.mcp-capi.svc:8080/mcp), and this reconcile drops the list whole — 4 server entries, 1 exchange target and 1 identity provider go, muster registers the shared defaults' servers alone, and everyone who reaches the others through kestrel's muster loses them. Move the registry to the hub first, register a server of its own as an MCPServer object under extras/agent-platform/mcpservers/, which a reconcile keeps, or force the join (forceJoin; platformctl --force-join), which proceeds with the warning
  Files (1 update, 30 unchanged):
    CHANGE  REPOSITORY                   PATH
    update  giantswarm/oakridge-configs  installations/kestrel/apps/agent-platform/configmap-values.yaml.patch
  Warning: this reconcile changes what kestrel's muster serves beyond the shared defaults:
    exchange targets removed: plover
    identity providers removed: plover
    MCP servers removed: kestrel/kubernetes http://mcp-kubernetes.mcp-kubernetes.svc:8080/mcp (its own); kestrel/prometheus http://mcp-prometheus.mcp-prometheus.svc:8080/mcp (its own); kestrel/capi http://mcp-capi.mcp-capi.svc:8080/mcp (its own); plover/kubernetes https://mcp-kubernetes.plover.oakridge.example/mcp
    public-registration redirect URIs removed: https://gateway.oakridge.example/oauth/callback (moved to heron)
  Includes: giantswarm/oakridge-management-clusters:management-clusters/kestrel/extras/kustomization.yaml resources ./agent-platform/ (unchanged)
